----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and use the traceroute command to trace the path packets take to a destination.
Tools Required: Kali Linux, terminal, internet connection.
Theory:
Traceroute is a network diagnostic tool that shows the route (path) packets take from source
to destination. It uses ICMP or UDP packets with increasing TTL (Time To Live) values.
Each router that decrements TTL to zero sends back an ICMP "Time Exceeded" message,
revealing its IP address.
Procedure:
1. Basic traceroute:
traceroute example.com
2. Traceroute using ICMP:
traceroute -I example.com
3. Traceroute using TCP:
sudo traceroute -T example.com
4. Limit hops:
traceroute -m 10 example.com
5. Traceroute to Metasploitable2:
traceroute 192.168.56.101
